Third-party components
----------------------

Binary distributions of siwx-oidc, including the container image, statically
link third-party Rust crates, each under its own license. The exact versions
are recorded in Cargo.lock. The container image carries their license texts
in /usr/share/licenses/siwx-oidc/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES-rust.txt, generated at
build time (see about.toml).

The following crates are licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0. They
are used unmodified, and the source code of each is available at
https://crates.io/crates/<name>:

    crypto-glue
    webauthn-attestation-ca
    webauthn-rs
    webauthn-rs-core
    webauthn-rs-proto

The web frontend in the container image is built from npm packages, each under
its own license. The exact versions are recorded in js/ui/package-lock.json.
The license texts of the packages bundled into it are served with it at
/build/third-party-licenses.txt and carried in the container image in
/usr/share/licenses/siwx-oidc/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES-js.txt.

The container image is built on Alpine Linux 3.24.2 (base image pinned by
digest in the Dockerfile). Its packages carry their own licenses, recorded with
each package in /lib/apk/db/installed; BusyBox and apk-tools, for example, are
licensed under GPL-2.0-only. The image carries the text of every license those
packages declare in /usr/share/licenses/alpine/. The Alpine packages are used
unmodified.

The corresponding source code of those packages is published by the Alpine
Linux project:

    Build recipes (aports), tag v3.24.2:
    https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/v3.24.2
    Each package's exact aports commit is its "c:" line in /lib/apk/db/installed.

    Upstream source archives those recipes build from:
    https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/v3.24/
